.TH MEMPOOL_CREATE_FROM_PREALLOCATED_BUFFER 3 "2026-08-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
mempool_create_from_preallocated_buffer \- create pool from user buffer
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cmempool.h>

mempool *mempool_create_from_preallocated_buffer(
    void *buffer,
    size_t buf_size,
    size_t elem_size,
    bool fallback_to_dynamic_memory,
    bool single_threaded,
    ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mmgmt_procs,
    char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a memory pool using a user-provided buffer instead of allocating
from the heap. Useful for embedded systems or when heap allocation is
undesirable.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
buffer                     Pointer to preallocated buffer
buf_size                   Size of buffer in bytes
elem_size                  Size of each element in bytes (must be > 0;
                          if smaller than sizeof(uintptr_t) it is rounded
                          up, mirroring mempool_create(); maximum
                          SIZE_MAX minus the internal header overhead)
fallback_to_dynamic_memory If true, allocate from heap when pool exhausted
single_threaded           If true, omit locking
mmgmt_procs               Custom memory management, or NULL
err                       Optional pointer to receive error string
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to newly created memory pool on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Element count is calculated as buf_size / stride, where stride is
  elem_size + header_overhead further rounded up so every element in the
  pool is correctly aligned, not just the first (the same stride
  DECLARE_PREALLOCATED_MEMPOOL_BUFFER sizes its own buffer with)
Buffer is not freed by mempool_destroy() (user manages buffer lifetime)
Pool struct itself is still allocated via mmgmt_procs
Returns NULL with error if elem_size is zero
If elem_size is nonzero but < sizeof(uintptr_t), it is rounded up
  (same as mempool_create())
Returns NULL with error if elem_size would overflow size_t once the
header overhead and alignment rounding are added
Returns NULL with error if buffer is not sufficiently aligned for the
  pool's internal per-element header (a size_t plus a pointer); a buffer
  declared via DECLARE_PREALLOCATED_MEMPOOL_BUFFER is always properly
  aligned, a hand-rolled buffer must be aligned to at least
  _Alignof(max_align_t)
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR DECLARE_PREALLOCATED_MEMPOOL_BUFFER (3),
.BR mempool_create (3),
.BR mempool_destroy (3)
